# Nowhere to Run: its own enters trigger targets "a creature an opponent controls" and the static ability is already in
# force when the trigger is put on the stack, so Bot2's hexproof Sylvan Caryatid (0/3) is a legal target and the -3/-3 kills
# it (CR 702.11b, 609.4). The refusal before the cast is the positive control: with no Nowhere to Run on the battlefield,
# Bot1's own Lightning Bolt cannot be aimed at the Caryatid. Bot2's Elvish Mystic, not hexproof, is a second candidate and
# lives, so the trigger took the target it was told to.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Nowhere to Run
Lightning Bolt
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Sylvan Caryatid
Elvish Mystic
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sylvan Caryatid.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Sylvan Caryatid)
Bot1.Hand.Nowhere to Run.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Sylvan Caryatid)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Sylvan Caryatid
Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Nowhere to Run.Types = Enchantment
